## Caption (Generated)

Architecture diagram showing Acme's platform service dependencies. The API Gateway routes traffic to five backend services: Auth, Projects, Assets, Wiki, and Task. All data services connect to the primary PostgreSQL database with two read replicas. The Assets service has additional storage dependencies (Supabase Storage). The Task service uses a Redis cache for session state. Background jobs run asynchronously against the same database and storage layers. An external CDN sits in front of the API Gateway for static assets.

## Key Services

| Service | Namespace | Upstream Dependencies | Downstream Consumers |
|---------|-----------|----------------------|---------------------|
| api-gateway | platform | CDN | All API services |
| auth-service | platform | postgres-auth | api-gateway |
| projects-service | services | postgres-primary | api-gateway |
| assets-service | services | postgres-primary, storage | api-gateway, background-jobs |
| wiki-service | services | postgres-primary | api-gateway |
| task-service | services | postgres-primary, redis | api-gateway |
| background-jobs | jobs | postgres-primary, storage, llm-apis | (async, no direct consumers) |
